  "narrative": [
    {
      "text": "Random Matrix Theory for the Hermitian Wilson Dirac Operator and the chGUE – GUE Transition — We introduce a random two-matrix model interpolating between a chiral Hermitian (2n + ν) × (2n+ν) matrix\n\n**Random Matrix Theory for the Hermitian Wilson Dirac Operator and the chGUE – GUE Transition**\n\n*Gernot Akemann1 and Taro Nagao2*\n\n27 pp, 15 sections.\n\n**Abstract.** We introduce a random two-matrix model interpolating between a chiral Hermitian (2n + ν) × (2n+ν) matrix and a second Hermitian matrix without symmetries. These are taken from the chiral Gaussian Unitary Ensemble (chGUE) and Gaussian Unitary Ensemble (GUE), respectively. In the microscopic large-n limit in the vicinity of the chGUE (which we denote by weakly non-chiral limit) this theory is in one to one correspondence to the partition function of Wilson chiral perturbation theory in the epsilon regime, such as the related two matrix-model previously introduced in [20, 21]. For a generic number of ﬂavours and rectangular block matrices in the chGUE part we derive an eigenvalue representation for the partition function displaying a Pfaﬃan structure.\n\n**Outline.** Front matter; 1 Introduction; 2 The Random Matrix Model; 3 The eigenvalue picture; 4 All density correlation functions for finite; 5 The microscopic weakly non-chiral large-N li; 6 Conclusions; A Equivalence to the partition function of Wch; A.1 Alternative representation of Nf=1 WchPT; B Consistency checks of the partition function; B.1 The GUE limit a1 for =0; B.2 The chGUE limit a0 and factorisation; C Skew-orthogonal polynomials; C.1 Expectation value of a single characterist; C.2 The odd polynomials R2j+1(x)",
      "lang": "en",
